From a320f21a8962f2a8152c65d017054cd8581f6bb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernt Budde <bernt.budde@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:44:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 62/85] Lexer: the loop variable of foreach is any of perl's
 forms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

perly.y's foreach reads, between the for word and the ( LIST ), an
optional my/our/state, an optional \ (refaliasing), and then a scalar,
a dereference ($$f, ${$r}, ${*$f}) or, after my, a list of
scalars (5.36's for my ($q, $r) (LIST)).  _continues knew only
[my] $scalar: a dereference reached "Illegal state in 'for' compound
statement" and PPI::Document->new returned undef for the whole file,
and the other forms ended the compound after its first word, so the
loop and the statement after it became one flat statement.

One helper, _foreach_head, walks the head so far: declarators and
casts keep it open, a symbol, a block after a cast or a () after my
completes it, and then only ( LIST ) or qw() may follow.
Anything else hands back to the rules that were there.  A compound
whose first word after for is a cast is of type foreach.

Regression pair 61_foreach_variable (the plans of 08_regression.t and
25_increment.t enumerate the directory).  Fixes PCL §6, §10 and §29 in
t/ppi_bugs_pcl.t; the for $$$r row stays TODO (a tokenizer row: the
tokenizer reads $$$r as $$ + $r).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
